 "text": "Hi there, how you doing? Sure, a complementary color is one that has the opposite color temperature from your main color. For example, if you shoot in warm light, use cool colors for the compliment. It' important for blending and keeping a smooth gradient. If you use the same color for light and shadow, the blended edge can look conspicuous. Yes, that's one way to approach it. Black is too strong to be complemented by, so something neutral, like a gray pen, is easier to blend. Grey pens are much more forgiving to use with color markers.",
